==Trivia==
*The word "''Barbarian''" comes from the Greek "''βάρβαρος''" (''bárbaros''), meaning foreign. Dating back to the ancient Greek times, the Greeks referred to non-Greek people as barbarians because the language they spoke sounded to Greeks like gibberish represented by the sounds "''bar... bar...''". 
**According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=Barb_Barrel_ColourWeb2.jpg strip], the Barbarians follow a career path, with the Barbarians being the second highest ranking ones.
*The Barbarians are 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The Barbarians resemble the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Barbarian Level 1-2 Barbarian] from Clash of Clans.
*The Barbarians are 1 of 3 troops which can be spawned by a troop (Barbarians/[[Battle Ram]]), a [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] ([[Barbarian Barrel]]), and a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] ([[Barbarian Hut]]). The others are Goblins and Skeletons.
*The Barbarians are one of the first troops to be featured in Clash-A-Rama, alongside the Minions, Goblins, and Giant.
*The Barbarians are one of the first troop [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Barbarians are one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Barbarians are one of the first troop cards to receive a [[Card Evolution]], alongside the Skeletons, [[Royal Giant]], and [[Firecracker]].
*Even though the card spawns 5 Barbarians, the card render displays only 1 Barbarian.
*The Barbarian bears more than a passing resemblance to [[wikipedia:Hulk_Hogan|Hulk Hogan]] and [https://walkingdead.fandom.com/wiki/Abraham_Ford_(TV_Series) Abraham Ford] from [https://walkingdead.fandom.com/wiki/The_Walking_Dead_(TV_Series) The Walking Dead TV series].
*From the Knight's description, it is implied that Knight and the Barbarians are distant cousins, due to their physical similarities, especially the color of their hair and mustaches. Coincidentally, both the Knight and Barbarians are voice acted by [https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1423395/ John Mondelli]. 
**The [[Electro Wizard]] and the [[Lumberjack]] are also voice acted by John Mondelli.
*The Barbarians' swords can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
*The Barbarians are 1 of 2 troops that has been featured in the [[Obstacle Course]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the other being Fisherman.
**The Barbarian in the Obstacle Course game mode looked like a rock guitarist player that would boost the speed of incoming troops for a few seconds.
*The Barbarians are featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Barbarians are featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Pins?file=Barbarian_Pin-Angry.png a pin in Brawl Stars] after Clash of Clans' 10th anniversary.
**The Barbarians, along with the Archers, Goblins, Elite Barbarians, and P.E.K.K.A, were featured as a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Monster monster] in [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_%26_Dragons_Wiki Puzzles and Dragons], in a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Dungeon dungeon] called [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Dungeon Clash of Clans Dungeon].
**The Barbarians, along with the Goblins, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, and the Archer Queen, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess].
**The Barbarians, along with the Archers, Goblins, Musketeer, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Miner, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
**The Barbarians are featured as a trophy in [https://mocosupercell.fandom.com/wiki/Mo.co_Wiki Mo.co].
**While not available as a character, the Barbarian's sounds, along with the Knight, Wizard, and [[Dark Prince]], were featured in the [https://beatstar.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_Royale_Theme Clash Royale Theme] [https://beatstar.fandom.com/wiki/Songs song] in [https://beatstar.fandom.com/wiki/Main_Page Beatstar].
*The Barbarians, along with the Archers, Goblins, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, Prince, and Night Witch, are featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Goblins, Skeletons, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and [[Princess]], they are also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*The Barbarian is featured on the card renders of the [[Zap]], [[Earthquake]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Clone]], and [[Mirror]].
*In [[Pass Royale|Fisherman's Float]] and Shipwreck Island, Barbarians can be seen sitting in the audience.
*It is said that Barbarians cannot function without their swords. This is referenced a few times:
**The Duelist [[Battle Banners|Decoration]] saying "''Swords. Barbarians don't enter the Arena without them!''"
**The [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Raged_Barbarian Raged Barbarian]'s description in Clash of Clans which says "''Why is he so angry, speedy, and vicious? Nobody's brave enough to ask. Maybe it's because he can't find his sword?''"
**In the Clash-A-Rama episode "[https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/%22Ballad_of_the_Barbarian%22 Ballad of the Barbarian]", a Barbarian was depressed because he lost his sword.
*There is a [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] that says: "''Don't feed Barbarian after midnight.''" This is a reference to [https://gremlins.fandom.com/wiki/Gremlins_Wiki Gremlins].
*The Barbarians are the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Barbarians are the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Barbarians are the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
***The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Emotes?file=Barbarian_Pixel_Frenzy.png Barbarian Pixel Frenzy Emote] is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong Donkey Kong].
*The Barbarians were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxEzjdKQ4HA Clash Royale Helsinki Tournament], by a player called Jason.
*Before the Barbarians' card release, the Barbarians' hitpoints were increased by 24%, and their damage was decreased by 12%.

